  "instagram": {
    "caption": "She doesn't plan the tower. She just grabs the next tile.\n\nI'd been saving my client presentation for a quiet afternoon. With a toddler, that afternoon doesn't exist. So I typed it into FOCO, tapped once, and it broke it down into tiny steps. Two steps done in 8 minutes, and she never looked up from her tower.\n\nWhat's the task you keep saving for a quiet afternoon? 👇",
    "hashtags": [
      "#adhdmom",
      "#momswithadhd",
      "#workfromhomemom",
      "#adhdtips",
      "#freelancemom"
    ],
    "altText": "Real home photos: a toddler stacks a tall magnet-tile tower next to her mom's open laptop. The mom has been putting off a client presentation due Friday. A real FOCO screenshot shows the presentation broken into small steps, with step 1 circled and an arrow to the tower: 1 step = 1 tile. She finishes two steps in 8 minutes and ends with the presentation started and the tower still standing. Ends with the FOCO app and App Store and Google Play badges."
  },
